# Pytest marker expression for a "core data plane" s3-tests run against fbs-core.
#
# Non-comment lines are joined with " and " (see run.sh build_marker_expr).
# Rationale for each clause: compat/s3-tests/markers.md
# Product scope: plan/s3-compatibility.md, plan/access-control/access-control.md
#
# Status tags in comments below:
#   noise              — not a useful fbs-core signal
#   permanent non-goal — product law (especially mini-IAM vs AWS IAM)
#   out of scope       — hard mismatch with single-node / no external services
#   deferred           — not implemented; may drop this line when the feature ships
#
# Mini-IAM grants (Management API) are NOT the same as AWS IAM/policy/STS markers.
# Shipping grants does not mean removing iam_* / bucket_policy / STS exclusions.

# --- noise ---
not fails_on_aws

# --- data management (deferred unless noted) ---
not versioning
not delete_marker
not lifecycle
not lifecycle_expiration
not lifecycle_transition
not object_lock
not tagging
not storage_class
not appendobject
not s3select

# --- AWS access-control protocol (permanent non-goal; see mini-IAM plan) ---
not bucket_policy
not object_ownership
not user_policy
not role_policy
not group_policy
not session_policy
not iam_role
not iam_user
not iam_account
not iam_cross_account
not iam_tenant
not test_of_sts
not webidentity_test
not abac_test

# --- encryption (deferred; SSE-KMS authz is non-goal) ---
not encryption
not sse_s3
not bucket_encryption

# --- website (not core data-plane) ---
not s3website
not s3website_routing_rules
not s3website_redirect_location

# --- logging & notifications ---
not bucket_logging
not bucket_logging_cleanup
not fails_without_logging_rollover
not sns

# --- cloud / S3 Control ---
not cloud_transition
not cloud_restore
not s3control

# --- auth protocol ---
not auth_aws2
